// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Source File : texts/Working 	Sheet : P_Tutorial_Dr_Steffard 
//
// Script      : Xlstocontactdef.bat 
// Version     : 35 
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Contact Name : Dr. Steffard 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Name :
"P2966469622" "Dr. Steffard"
// LocationString :
// ProfessionString :
"P613835953" "Scientist"
// DescriptionString :
"P1703482758" "Dr. Steffard is a scientist specializing in super powered individuals. His interest is more than passing, as he's an expert in the details of how a super can tap into that power."
// IntroString :
// TaskDeclineOverride :
"P1071114353" "Wait, wait, start over again."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - DrSteffardDialog 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Blowoff Text :
"P70088369" "Hello {HeroName}, I'm tickled pink that you'd come talk to me without having any particular reason to do so.<br><br>Perhaps you've come to hear some of my dissertations on inter-origin power deconstruction?  No?  Perhaps my grand unifying theory on hero costumes?  Not that either?  It has a really good bit about the deficiencies of capes.  No?  Well I guess I won't waste anymore of your time."
// Answer Text :
"P2420087866" "Goodbye."
// Page Intro Text :
"P1671941413" "Hello. I'm Dr. Steffard.<br><br>My research on super powered individuals is indeed extensive, my resume vast, I have extrapolated theoretical super powered beings that were then found to exist in the wild!<br><br>My theories on {HeroOrigin} supers of course predicted you could exist; so I know everything about how your powers work.  I..."
// Answer Text :
"P431419551" "I uhh... gotta run.  Thanks for... whatever that was."
// Answer Text :
"P3978422075" "(Optional) The Interrogator said you could tell me more about my powers."
// Answer Text :
"P1968930538" "(Optional) These powers are a mess, I need organization!"
// Answer Text :
"P2697061358" "(Optional) How do I not die while 'defending the peace'?"
// Page PowersInfoBlaster Text :
"P3558235145" "Your {HeroOrigin} powers are just {Hero.gender=Male sparking|budding} right now.<br><br>For instance, as a <color red>Blaster</color>, you can still use the first two powers of your primary set and the first power of your secondary set while you are held, stunned, or slept. Additionally, whenever you hit with a power, you gain a stacking damage bonus to subsequent attacks for short time.<br><br><color orange>"
// Answer Text :
"P1036764897" "Thanks for the referesher, doc. I'll be on my way now."
// Answer Text :
"P1868726805" "(Optional) But these powers are a mess, I need organization!"
// Answer Text :
"P2120252278" "(Optional) So how do I not die while 'defending the peace'?"
// Page PowersInfoDominator Text :
"P147775922" "Your {HeroOrigin} powers are just {Hero.gender=Male sparking|budding} right now.<br><br>For instance, as a <color mediumvioletred>Dominator</color>, some of your stronger foes will be resistant to your control powers and you may have to use a power multiple times before it affects that foe. But when your Domination bar is over 90%, you can activate your <color mediumvioletred>Domination</color> power, doubling the magnitude of your control powers and making it easier to lock down enemies for even longer, as well as refilling your <color dodgerblue>endurance</color> and breaking you free from control effects that are on you.<br><br><color orange>"
// Page PowersInfoBrute Text :
"P2789274625" "Your {HeroOrigin} powers are just {Hero.gender=Male sparking|budding} right now.<br><br>For instance, as a <color steelblue>Brute</color>, your FURY increases your attack power. Your fury bar increases the more you attack and get attacked.<br><br><color orange>Your powers <b><color red>tray</b></color> contains an icon for each of your powers.  Left click an icon to use a power, or right click on it to learn about the power.<br><img src=Tut_P_TrayWSprintOn.tga><br>Try right clicking on Sprint to learn more about it, and left clicking on it to turn it on.</color>"
// Page PowersInfoTanker Text :
"P1971460799" "Your {HeroOrigin} powers are just {Hero.gender=Male sparking|budding} right now.<br><br>For instance, as a <color lightsteelblue>Tanker</color>, you're the the frontline of defense on teams. Your inherent Gauntlet power will draw enemies to attack you with each attack you deliver.<br><br><color orange>"
// Page PowersInfoMastermind Text :
"P103406056" "Your {HeroOrigin} powers are just {Hero.gender=Male sparking|budding} right now.<br><br>For instance, as a <color chartreuse>Mastermind</color>, you can not only summon other creatures to do your bidding, but you also have special powers to help control your henchmen. Additionally, if you have line of sight to your underlings and they are within 60 feet, they gain a bonus to accuracy and damage. You can set any of your minions to Bodyguard by right-clicking them, selecting the Defensive stance and then using the Follow, Goto, or Stay order. This causes your pets to absorb some of the damage you take.<br><br><color orange>Your powers tray contains an icon for each of your powers.  Left click an icon to use a power, or right click on it to learn about the power.<br><span align=center>"
// Page PowersInfoController Text :
"P1885002615" "Your {HeroOrigin} powers are just {Hero.gender=Male sparking|budding} right now.<br><br>For instance, as a <color magenta>Controller</color>, your control powers let you keep your foes from operating at their maximum efficiency. However, some of your stronger foes will be resistant to your control powers and you may have to use a power multiple times before it affects that foe. Also, whenever you have a foe held, immobilized, slept, or stunned, you deal additional damage to that foe.<br><br><color orange>"
// Page PowersInfoDefender Text :
"P2013841976" "Your {HeroOrigin} powers are just {Hero.gender=Male sparking|budding} right now.<br><br>For instance, as a <color dodgerblue>Defender</color> while you are working with a team, you can use your powers at a decreased <color dodgerblue>endurance</color> cost if your allies are badly damaged.  Conversely, the smaller the team you are on, the greater damage you are able to do.<br><br><color orange>"
// Page PowersInfoCorruptor Text :
"P687443570" "Your {HeroOrigin} powers are just {Hero.gender=Male sparking|budding} right now.<br><br>For instance, as a <color crimson>Corruptor</color>, you have the Scourge ability.  When a foe has 50% health or less, you gain a chance of dealing double damage with every attack.<br><br><color orange>"
// Page PowersInfoScrapper Text :
"P3762116947" "Your {HeroOrigin} powers are just {Hero.gender=Male sparking|budding} right now.  For instance, you have a 5% chance to deal double damage against any target when using your <color orange>Scrapper</color> attacks.  This chance increases to 10% against Lieutenants, Bosses and stronger foes.<br><br><color orange>"
// Answer Text :
"P2534957931" "(Optional) That's all well, but my powers tray is disorganized."
// Page PowersInfoStalker Text :
"P2886273429" "Your {HeroOrigin} powers are just {Hero.gender=Male sparking|budding} right now. For instance, if you haven't already turned on your <color lightslategray>Hide</color> power, I would do so now. Whenever you are in a threatening situation, Hide should be on. Hide lets you make <color red>critical hits</color> on targets that are unaware of you and lets you <color lightslategray>avoid detection</color> before you are ready to strike.<br><br>Be careful: taking damage or making attacks will allow others to detect you.<br><br><color orange>"
// Page PowersTab Text :
"P1003419496" "You can click the powers tab above the tray to drag new powers to the tray. You can reorganize the powers in your tray by dragging the icons around.<br><br><br><img src=Tut_P_PowersTrayOpen.tga>"
// Answer Text :
"P3605070780" "That's much better. Thanks."
// Answer Text :
"P4246350801" "(Optional) Ah, that helps. So how do I not die while 'defending the peace'?"
// Page Medicom Text :
"P1665667995" "Ah, do not worry.  When you joined the Powers Division, you were tagged by the <color orange>Medicom</color>.<br><br>The Medicom monitors your current medical status at all times, and if you are defeated, it can instantly transport you to the nearest medical facility where you will enjoy a speedy recovery.<br><br>Of course, if you have a nearby associate who can revive you, you can wait for that instead by just not clicking <color red>Go to Hospital</color>.<br><span align=center><img src=Tut_P_GotoHospital.tga>"
// Answer Text :
"P239052739" "What a relief. I really should be going."
// Answer Text :
"P1118476342" "Glad to hear it. How reliable are these Medicoms?"
// Page SendToInterrogator Text :
"P2793972691" "Quite reliable.  Why, once you have had a Medicom frequency applied to you, it cannot be undone.  So no matter what, even if you left the Powers Division, you would still be covered.<br><br>...Of course if you traveled to another dimension or something, it probably wouldn't work.  Unless they somehow had an identical Medicom system.  But that's highly unlikely unless that dimension was a near-mirror of this one.<br><br>Some people surmise that these devices are so advanced that they must be alien technology!  This is nonsense, as the technology was developed by Dr. Keyes himself, a brilliant...<br><br>...<br><br>Sorry, here I am talking away at you, you probably have other things you need to do right now."
// Answer Text :
// Page JustSignThePapers Text :
"P1443567393" "Sorry, here I am talking away at you, you probably have other things you need to do right now."
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 


