// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Source File : texts/Working 	Sheet : P_Tutorial_Interrogator_Hoffman 
//
// Script      : Xlstocontactdef.bat 
// Version     : 35 
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Contact Name : Interrogator Hoffman 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Name :
"P3446115600" "Interrogator Hoffman"
// LocationString :
// ProfessionString :
"P3963473481" "Interrogator"
// DescriptionString :
"P127261120" "Interrogator Hoffman is an expert in extracting data and technology from the Resistance. He's confiscated several clockwork that were reprogrammed by the Resistance and has been attempting to figure out how they managed to hack in."
// IntroString :

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - HoffmanDialog 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Blowoff Text :
"P1694071680" "Hello {HeroName}, glad to have you on our side.<br><br>I'm sure you have better things to do than chat with me, so I won't waste your time."
// Answer Text :
"P2724641317" "Thanks."
// Page Intro Text :
"P4248805447" "Hello {HeroName}, glad to have you on our side.<br><br>Feel free to test out your powers on one of these broken clockwork, <color red>but I am sure you have other things to do</color>.<br><br><color orange>Click on a clockwork to select it, then hit F to get in range.<br><br>You can use the number keys above the letters on your keyboard to activate the powers in your tray.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P2208595181" "(Optional) What's wrong with these clockwork?"
// Answer Text :
"P260085503" "(Optional) I can't attack fast enough."
// Answer Text :
"P4121132605" "(Optional) These guys are real pushovers."
// Page ResistanceClockwork Text :
"P1890449668" "The Resistance sometimes hacks our clockwork and turns them against us. I have a few clockwork here that were reclaimed from the Resistance. Unfortunately, in my attempt to retrieve data from them, they seized up into this malfunctioning mode that wiped their memory.<br><br>They're useless now."
// Answer Text :
"P4087439994" "I have a great use for them. Target practice."
// Page TalkAboutRecharge Text :
"P3756534003" "You can't just attack non-stop.  That's because all powers have a recharge time.<br><br>When you use a power, it goes dark until it recharges.  If you attempt to use it before it finishes recharging, you will queue it up for use as your next attack.<br><br>The simple powers you have right now have relatively short recharge times.  Powers you earn later in your career are more powerful, but take longer to recharge.<br><br><span align=center><img src=Tut_P_PowerRecharging.tga>"
// Answer Text :
"P3944581003" "Ok, I get it."
// Page TalkAboutConning Text :
"P4139598214" "True, but you will meet tougher enemies. There are three basic ranks:<br><br><b>Minions</b>, like these, are the weakest and are easiest to defeat.<br><b><color #FFFF00>Lieutenants</color></b> are stronger, and have more attacks.<br><b><color #ff9900>Bosses</color></b> are the strongest and are particularly resistant to status effects. You may need backup when fighting a boss.<br><br><br>When you target an enemy or ally, you can note the difficulty of that target by the color of the name.</b><br><br><color DarkGray><b>Gray</b></color> names mean the enemy is quite weak and worth no rewards.<br><b><color LawnGreen>Green</b></color> and <b><color dodgerblue>Blue</b></color> names mean they are weak and give minor rewards.<br><b>White</b> means they are the same level as yourself and give normal rewards.<br><b><color #ffff00>Yellow</color></b>, <b><color DarkOrange>Orange</color></b>, and <b><color red>Red</color></b> names are enemies that are tougher than you.<br><br><b><color Magenta>Purple</color></b> names mean enemies that are vastly superior to you. If you train hard and hone your powers, you may eventually be able to take on purples."
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 


